@startuml
' Figure 4.6 – System sequence diagram: inline AI edit on a text selection
!include ../_style.puml
mainframe interaction SequenceDiagram Inline AI action
autonumber "0 :"

participant "Writer" as R
participant "Editor" as W
participant "System" as A
participant "Language\nmodel" as L
participant "Database" as D

ref over R, D : Sign in

R -> W : Select text in the article
activate W
W -> W : Capture the selected range once
R -> W : Choose an action\n(reformulate, shorten, expand, simplify, improve)
W -> A : POST /ai/inline with the selection and the action
activate A
A -> D : Read and grant the daily allowance
activate D
D --> A : Remaining tokens
deactivate D

alt allowance exhausted
  A --> W : 402 with the plan-aware notice
  W --> R : Offer the upgrade path
else allowance available
  A -> A : Build the prompt from the action, the selection\nand the surrounding article
  A -> L : Stream a completion
  activate L
  loop for each generated chunk
    L --> A : Chunk
    A --> W : Server-sent event
    W --> R : Preview the suggestion as it arrives
  end
  L --> A : End of stream and tokens consumed
  deactivate L
  A -> D : Record the interaction and decrement the balance
  A --> W : Completed suggestion
  alt the writer accepts
    R -> W : Replace, or insert below
    W -> W : Apply the edit to the captured range
  else the writer declines
    R -> W : Cancel
  end
end
deactivate A
deactivate W

note over R, D
  The range is captured once, before the stream starts. Reading
  the selection again after the stream let any click or blur move
  it, so "Replace" could silently overwrite different text.
end note
@enduml
